{
  "slug": "auto-memory",
  "name": "Auto Memory",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Automatically maintains CLAUDE.md files as codebases evolve using hooks, agents, and skills",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills**, **1 agent**, **4 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (2): `codebase-analyzer` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"initialize auto-memory\", \"create CLAUDE.md\", \"set up project memory\",…), `memory-processor` (Process file changes and update CLAUDE.md memory sections)\n- **Agents** (1): `memory-updater` (Orchestrates CLAUDE.md updates for changed files)\n- **Commands** (4): `calibrate` (Force recalibration of all CLAUDE.md files), `init` (Initialize CLAUDE.md memory structure for project with interactive wizard), `status` (Show CLAUDE.md memory sync status), `sync` (Sync CLAUDE.md with manual file changes detected by git)\n- **Hooks** (4): `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `SubagentStop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install auto-memory@claude-community` from `severity1/claude-code-auto-memory`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 2,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 4
  },
